<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Eelgrass/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Eelgrass/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Eelgrass/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Eelgrass'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Eelgrass is a common name for Zostera - a small genus of widely distributed seagrasses. Zostera is found on sandy substrates or in estuaries submerged or partially floating. Most Zostera are perennial. They have long, bright green, ribbon-like leaves, about 1 cm wide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Eelgrass'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Electric/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Electric/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Electric/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Electric Utilities'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Electric utilities are the infrastructure needed in the generation, transmission, and distribution of electricity to a community.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Electric'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Employment/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Employment/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Employment/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Employment'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Patterns of job availability and job sector diversity in a local economy.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Employment'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Erosion/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Erosion/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Erosion/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Erosion'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Erosion is the carrying away or displacement of solids (sediment, soil, rock and other particles) usually by the agents of currents such as, wind, water, or ice by downward or down-slope movement in response to gravity. Erosion is an intrinsic natural process but in many places it is increased by human land use. Poor land use practices include deforestation, overgrazing, unmanaged construction activity and other activities that involve removal of vegetation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Erosion'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Estuary/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Estuary/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Estuary/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Estuary'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An estuary is a semi-enclosed coastal body of water with one or more rivers or streams flowing into it, where salt water is measurably diluted with fresh water from the land. Estuaries are often associated with high rates of biological productivity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Estuary'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryClassifications/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryClassifications/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryClassifications/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Estuary classifications'@en ;
    skos:definition 'To maintain diversity among Oregon\'s estuaries, Goal 16 directs the Land Conservation and Development Commission to set overall limits on the amount of development that can occur in each estuary. The classification sets an upper limit on the types and intensities of development that can occur and serves as a guide to preparation of plans for each estuary.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::EstuaryClassifications'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryManagementUnits/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryManagementUnits/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryManagementUnits/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Estuary Management Units'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Estuary plans divide each estuary into a number of different zones or areas called management units. Management units are discrete geographic areas, defined by biophysical characteristics and features, within which particular uses and activities are promoted, encouraged, protected, or enhanced, and others are discouraged, restricted, or prohibited. Estuary plans identify appropriate uses for each estuary management unit. Goals 16 directs what kinds of areas are to be included in each management unit and what kinds of uses can be allowed in each type of management unit.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::EstuaryManagementUnits'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/FineGrained/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/FineGrained/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/FineGrained/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Fine-grained sandy beach'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Beach composed of fine sand: In USA, sand is commonly divided into five sub-categories based on size: very fine sand (1/16 - 1/8 mm diameter), fine sand (1/8 mm - 1/4 mm), medium sand (1/4 mm - 1/2 mm), coarse sand (1/2 mm - 1 mm), and very coarse sand (1 mm - 2 mm).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::FineGrained'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fire/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fire/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fire/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Fire Stations'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fire station is a structure or other area set aside for storage of firefighting apparatus (i.e, fire engines and related vehicles), personal protective equipment, firehose, fire extinguishers, and other fire extinguishing equipment.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Fire'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fishing/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fishing/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Fishing/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Fishing'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Fishing is the activity of hunting for fish by hooking (e.g. using trolls or longlines), trapping (e.g. using pots), or gathering (e.g. using trawls or seines).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Fishing'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flat/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flat/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flat/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Flat'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Flats are coastal wetlands that form when mud and sand is deposited by the tides or rivers, sea and oceans. They are broad mud flats which are exposed to the air at low tide and flooded by a mix of salt and fresh waters at high tide, found in sheltered areas such as bays, lagoons, and estuaries.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Flat'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flood/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flood/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Flood/>;
    dc:modified '2011-08-15T11:58:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Flood'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A flood is an overflow of an expanse of water that submerges land.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A02::Flood'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/ForestServiceLands/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/ForestServiceLands/1/>
